**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery Mission**

---

## 1. Goal Table

| Name                                                              | Text                                                                             | Runtime                  | Goal Type | Target Condition / Enquired Information          | Relation                 | Ground truth I | Ground truth C | Ground truth E |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------ | -------------- | -------------- | -------------- |
| **G1: Execute Resource Delivery Mission**                         | Achieve the delivery of all requested resources to the specified destination.    | `;` (sequential)         | Achieve   | All requested resources delivered to destination | AND (with G2 and G3)     |                |                |                |
| **G2: Collect Resources**                                         | Perform collection of resources from storage locations.                          | `FALLBACK(G2.1, G2.2)`   | Perform   | –                                                | AND (with G2.1 & G2.2)   |                |                |                |
| **G2.1: Normal Collection Process**                               | Collect resources from storage following estimated waiting time and path.        | `;`                      | Perform   | –                                                | AND (with AT1, AT2, AT3) |                |                |                |
| **G2.2: Handle Low Battery During Collection**                    | Return to recharging station and transfer mission to another robot.              | `;`                      | Perform   | –                                                | AND (with AT6, AT9)      |                |                |                |
| **G3: Deliver Resources**                                         | Perform delivery of collected resources to destination.                          | `FALLBACK(G3.1, G3.2)`   | Perform   | –                                                | AND (with G3.1 & G3.2)   |                |                |                |
| **G3.1: Normal Delivery Process**                                 | Deliver resources to the specified location.                                     | `;`                      | Perform   | –                                                | AND (with AT4, AT5)      |                |                |                |
| **G3.2: Handle Low Battery During Delivery**                      | Return resource to checkpoint and transfer remaining task to another robot.      | `FALLBACK(G3.2.1, G3.3)` | Perform   | –                                                | AND (with G3.2.1 & G3.3) |                |                |                |
| **G3.2.1: Return Resource to Checkpoint & Assign Remaining Task** | Return resource to checkpoint and hand over remaining delivery to another robot. | `;`                      | Perform   | –                                                | AND (with AT7, AT9)      |                |                |                |
| **G3.3: Failure to Return Resource to Checkpoint**                | Send alert to sector manager if resource cannot be returned to checkpoint.       | `-` (leaf)               | Perform   | –                                                | AND (with AT8)           |                |                |                |


---

## 2. Task Table

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|
| **AT1: Navigate to Storage** | Move robot to the storage location where the resource is located. | AND (under G2.1) | Storage | 1 |
| **AT2: Send Resource Request** | Send message to storage specifying requested resources. | AND (under G2.1) | Storage | 1 |
| **AT3: Wait for Resource Retrieval** | Wait until the requested resources are retrieved from storage. | AND (under G2.1) | Storage | 1 |
| **AT4: Navigate to Delivery Location** | Move robot to the destination where the resource must be delivered. | AND (under G3.1) | Delivery Location | 1 |
| **AT5: Deliver Resource** | Transfer the resource to the requesting agent at the destination. | AND (under G3.1) | Delivery Location | 1 |
| **AT6: Navigate to Recharging Station** | Move robot to the recharging station to replenish battery. | AND (under G2.2) | Recharging Station | 1 |
| **AT7: Return Resource to Checkpoint** | Return the resource to a checkpoint before handing over to another robot. | AND (under G3.2.1) | Checkpoint | 1 |
| **AT8: Send Alert to Sector Manager** | Trigger alert and send report to sector manager if resource cannot be returned to checkpoint. | AND (under G3.3) | Sector Manager Office | 1 |
| **AT9: Assign Mission to Another Robot** | Transfer remaining collection or delivery task to another robot and update mission assignment. | AND (under G2.2 & G3.2.1) | Current Location | 1 |

