## 4. Logical Relationships

```
G1 -> G2, G3 [AND][;]
G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [AND][FALLBACK(G2.1,G2.2)]
G2.1 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [AND][;]
G2.2 -> AT6, AT9 [AND][;]
G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [AND][FALLBACK(G3.1,G3.2)]
G3.1 -> AT4, AT5 [AND][;]
G3.2 -> G3.2.1, G3.3 [AND][FALLBACK(G3.2.1,G3.3)]
G3.2.1 -> AT7, AT9 [AND][;]
G3.3 -> AT8 [AND][-]
```

*Each `AND` indicates that all child nodes must be satisfied for the parent to be satisfied.  
The runtime annotations (`;`, `#`, `FALLBACK(...)`, `-`) describe the execution order over the children.*
